        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=3x+9$.",
          "worked": "The $y$-intercept is $9$. Using $(0,9)$ and $(-3,0)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}c&=9\\\\m&=\\frac{9-0}{0-(-3)}=\\frac93=3\\\\y&=3x+9\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-4x-7$.",
          "worked": "The $y$-intercept is $-7$. Using $(-1,-3)$ and $(0,-7)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}c&=-7\\\\m&=\\frac{-7-(-3)}{0-(-1)}=-\\frac41=-4\\\\y&=-4x-7\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\frac14x-3$.",
          "worked": "The $y$-intercept is $-3$. Using $(0,-3)$ and $(4,-2)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}c&=-3\\\\m&=\\frac{-2-(-3)}{4-0}=\\frac14\\\\y&=\\frac14x-3\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-2x+10$.",
          "worked": "The $y$-intercept is $10$. Using $(0,10)$ and $(5,0)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}c&=10\\\\m&=\\frac{0-10}{5-0}=-\\frac{10}{5}=-2\\\\y&=-2x+10\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
